 "question": "B. Is this measure already running in Åland (or in the Tyks university hospital area that treats its patients)?\nA. Does recent evidence support the size of effect we assume: does this measure shorten the time from first symptom to treatment start for lung cancer patients, and by how many days?\nMeasure: Reflex molecular testing ordered by pathology. The pathologist starts the biomarker panel (EGFR, ALK, ROS1, PD-L1, NGS) as soon as non-small cell lung cancer is seen, without waiting for the oncologist to order it. The result now decides treatment at every stage: osimertinib or alectinib after surgery, durvalumab or osimertinib after chemoradiotherapy in stage III, and the first drug in advanced disease.",
